          "pull_request": {
            "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/date-fns/date-fns/pulls/4337",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/date-fns/date-fns/pull/4337",
            "diff_url": "https://github.com/date-fns/date-fns/pull/4337.diff",
            "patch_url": "https://github.com/date-fns/date-fns/pull/4337.patch",
            "merged_at": null
          },
          "body": "`step: 0.5` leaves the date unchanged in `eachHourOfInterval`, causing an infinite loop. The Temporal version throws for fractional steps. Truncate the step before checking for zero and its sign, and document the whole-hour behavior.\n\nFixes #4336.\n\nValidation on Node 26.10.0: four new Temporal cases fail before the fix; 132 related hour/day/minute tests pass afterward with `--testTimeout15000`. The longer timeout accommodates an existing minute test that iterates from 2024 to `Date.now()`. Both implementations now return an empty array for sub-hour steps. Format and type-aware lint pass.\n",
          "reactions": {
            "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/date-fns/date-fns/issues/4337/reactions",
