          "pull_request": {
            "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/date-fns/date-fns/pulls/4352",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/date-fns/date-fns/pull/4352",
            "diff_url": "https://github.com/date-fns/date-fns/pull/4352.diff",
            "patch_url": "https://github.com/date-fns/date-fns/pull/4352.patch",
            "merged_at": null
          },
          "body": "`eachDayOfInterval`, `eachMonthOfInterval`, and `eachYearOfInterval` never advance with `step: 0.5` or `-0.5`, so they keep allocating dates without returning. Truncate the step before checking for zero and direction. Sub-unit steps return an empty array; larger fractional steps use whole calendar units. Apply the same normalization to the Temporal implementations and document it.\n\nRelated to #4336 and #4337, which address hour enumeration. This change covers day, month, and year enumeration; it does not duplicate the proposed hour fix or #4288's midnight handling.\n\nVerification:\n\n- A bounded Date-subclass reproduction stopped each original implementation after ten repeated iterations; all three now return `[]` without advancing the date.\n- Before the fix, the new larger-fraction tests had four Temporal failures and eight passes. Afterward, all 152 related Date/Temporal tests pass, including positive/negative fractions, sub-unit steps, existing reversed intervals, and time-zone contexts.\n- Node 26.10.0: `pnpm dlx node@26 ../../node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs run --project main --testTimeout 15000` from `pkgs/core` — 253 files / 3,160 tests passed, 19 skipped. Related tests also pass in Chromium: `run eachDayOfInterval eachMonthOfInterval eachYearOfInterval --browser --browser.headless` — 152 passed.\n- Node 24.16.0: all 76 related Date tests pass.\n- Changed-file `pnpm exec oxfmt`, type-aware `pnpm exec oxlint --type-aware`, and `git diff --check` pass. No dependency, version, or changelog changes.\n\nAI assistance: Codex authored the patch, tests, and description and ran the listed checks. No human review is claimed.\n\nGitHub Actions on head `89c5d23`: Node.js, Browser, Time zone, Smoke, and Code quality workflows all report `action_required`; they need maintainer approval to execute. These jobs have not run, so the results above are local validation.\n",
